Answer:
  Based on the provided context, anyone who has the right to vote in a local election or who meets the criteria for voting rights as outlined in the relevant sections of the law (such as being a citizen of Sweden or one of the European Union member states, having lived in Iceland or Norway for at least three years prior to the election day, or being born in Sweden and living there since July 1, 1995) qualifies to participate in a municipal referendum. Additionally, those who have been registered voters in their municipality must also be eligible to vote in such referendums. The specific requirements vary depending on whether the referendum takes place during regular elections or national referendums. In cases where the referendum coincides with general elections or national referendums, additional rules apply regarding registration and voter eligibility. However, generally speaking, any individual meeting these basic qualifications would qualify to cast a ballot in a municipal referendum.
