"Bestämmelserna gäller dock inte Försvarsmaktens användande av våld i enlighet med internationell rätt och sedvänja. Förordning (2006:153)."

This means that while Försvarsmaktens personnel cannot use violence internationally, they can use firearms when performing their duties as part of protecting themselves or others from immediate threats. However, this does not apply to using weapons against civilians or other individuals outside of official military operations. The context also mentions that these rules do not apply to internal security measures within the military itself. 

The key point here is that Försvarsmaktens personnel can use firearms only when necessary and authorized to do so, with specific conditions regarding protection of life and maintaining order. They must ensure that any use of force is proportional and justified by the circumstances at hand. This aligns with international norms and legal standards governing the use of lethal force in armed conflict situations.
